# Mark the moment (#551; marks v2 #574; the toggle #632 - each written before its implementation): on the simulated
# Index, ONE press of BOTH trackpads together STARTS a recording at once and the SAME press again STOPS and saves it
# (the owner, 2026-10-22: holding both trackpads blocked his thumbs, so the buttons could not be used while he talked).
# There is no hold any more and no snapshot-only short press: however long the start press is held, letting go changes
# nothing; the thumbs are free during the recording - a trackpad or a button pressed ALONE acts on the game as usual
# and does not stop it. A recording lasts at most 1 minute (marks.capMs); then it stops and saves by itself.
# What a recording writes is #574's hold, from the start press to the stop press (or the cap): left.png and right.png
# (both eyes of the start frame: the start's snapshot), recorder.txt, the left eye as snap-+NN.Ns.jpg every 2 s and at
# the stop, clip.vrsim (the replay ring from 10 s before the start to the stop, its "# hold: <startMs> <stopMs>" header
# line), meta.txt (kind=hold, pressMs = the start, releaseMs = the stop) and note.wav when a microphone recorded one
# (never here: the simulated headset opens no microphone - the note is tests/vr/VoiceNoteTest.h and the owner's
# headset test). The folder layout is unchanged, so scripts/dev/marks.ps1 and transcribe.ps1 read the new recordings
# as they read #574's holds. The indicator in the hero-dialogue panel (the subtitle panel of #460 / D-055) follows the
# RECORDING, with or without a microphone: "recording" ("<mic> m:ss" counting up) from the start for as long as it
# records, then "saved" ("... saved (m:ss)", the recording's length) once its files are written, fading quickly
# (about 1.5 s, as #574's "Note saved"). Both stick clicks held: no mark and no game menu (the D-058 fallback stays
# removed; menu-long-press.xrs has the radial's way to the menu). The feature's one CI sequence (coordinator Tests and
# CI rule 11): about 18 s after the load (#574's was about 19 s) - a 3 s recording ended by a shortened cap, then a
# 4.5 s one stopped by the second press, which needs 10 s of session before its start for its clip.
#
# Assumes (the worker adds them, named exactly; tests/vr/MarkMomentTest.h and tests/vr/MarkHoldTest.h have the pure
# helpers of #551/#574, which stay):
#   marks.count          (count)  recordings started since the start of the game (the stop press is no new one)
#   marks.last           (text)   the last mark's folder name: <yyyymmdd>T<hhmmss>Z-<n> (UTC, n = its number)
#   marks.lastFiles      (text)   the non-empty files in it, sorted by name, joined by "," without spaces
#   marks.lastKind       (text)   "" before the first mark; pending from the start press until the stop (the second
#                                 press or the cap); then hold - meta.txt's kind= of #574, kept so the folder layout
#                                 and marks.ps1 stay as they are. Never press for a new recording
#   marks.lastSnapshots  (number) the snap-*.jpg files written for the last mark so far
#   marks.lastClipMs     (number) the last mark's clip.vrsim length in ms (its last frame line's time less its first's)
#                                 once written
#   marks.recording      (bool)   NEW MEANING (#632): a recording is on - from the start press until the stop press or
#                                 the cap - with or without a microphone (#574: "a voice note records now")
#   marks.recordingMs    (number) NEW: how long the recording on now has run, ms; 0 when none is on
#   marks.capMs          (number) NEW: the longest recording, ms - 60000 (the owner: 1 minute). The test hook: the
#                                 channel's `marks cap <ms>` (NEW, next to `marks note on|off`) sets it for the session
#                                 (a whole number of ms from 1000 to 60000; anything else refused); a recording
#                                 reaching it stops and saves by itself as if the second press came then
#   marks.noteMs         (number) the voice note's length so far, ms; 0 when none records (always here: no microphone)
#   marks.note           (bool)   the voice note is on (cfg.ini vr_mark_note; the channel's `marks note on|off`)
#   marks.gesture        (text)   both.trackpad on the Index, none on a controller without trackpads (the Touch)
#   scene.subtitle.notice (text)  the notice the hero-dialogue panel shows: none | marked | recording | saved
#   log "[vr] mark #<n>: marks\<folder> files=<lastFiles>" once every file of the recording is written (after its
#   stop), and the panel's "vr.scene.subtitle notice=<marked|recording|saved> ... text="<the line>"" when a notice
#   shows
# The trackpads' bindings: free by default (D-042). One is bound to jump here (the channel's `vr-input bind`) to see a
# trackpad pressed alone act on the game during a recording; the default layout comes back at the end.
@sim idle
@save mvp-new-game
@args --loadslot 0

@until state eq GAMEPLAY 60s
@until vr.sim.timelineFrame ge 270 60s       # 3 s into the level: past its fade-in (TRAPS.md)
@assert player.controlsBlocked eq false
@assert vr.input.controllers eq index
@assert menuMode eq ingame
@assert player.inventoryOpen eq false
@assert marks.count eq 0
@assert marks.gesture eq both.trackpad
@assert marks.capMs eq 60000
@assert marks.recording eq false
@assert marks.recordingMs eq 0
@assert marks.noteMs eq 0
@assert marks.lastSnapshots eq 0
@assert marks.lastClipMs eq 0
@assert scene.subtitle.notice eq none
marks note off
@frames 2
@assert marks.note eq false
marks note on
@frames 2
@assert marks.note eq true

# 1. Both stick clicks held 2.5 s: nothing special - no mark, no game menu (past the removed fallback's 2 s)
vr-input down left.stick_click; vr-input down right.stick_click
@wait 2500
@assert marks.count eq 0
@assert menuMode eq ingame
vr-input up left.stick_click; vr-input up right.stick_click
@wait 300
@assert marks.count eq 0
@assert scene.subtitle.notice eq none
@assert menuMode eq ingame

# 2. The 1 minute cap, shortened to 3 s through the test hook. The left trackpad alone for 1 s: no mark; the right
# pressed too: the recording starts at once, the indicator on. The start press HELD 1.5 s (past #574's 0.5 s hold
# threshold) and let go: nothing changes - still recording, still pending (#574 ended a hold at its release). At 3 s
# it stops and saves by itself: the snapshots at 2 s and at the stop (3 s), the clip, "saved"
marks cap 3000
@frames 2
@assert marks.capMs eq 3000
@mark
vr-input down left.trackpad
@wait 1000
@assert marks.count eq 0
@assert marks.recording eq false
@assert scene.subtitle.notice eq none
vr-input down right.trackpad
@until marks.count eq 1 1s
@until marks.recording eq true 1s
@until scene.subtitle.notice eq recording 1s
@assert scene.subtitle.visible eq true
@assert scene.subtitle.drawn eq chest
@assert marks.lastKind eq pending
@assert menuMode eq ingame
@log vr\.scene\.subtitle notice=recording [^\n]*text="\S+ 0:0\d" 2s
@wait 1500
vr-input up left.trackpad; vr-input up right.trackpad
@wait 300
@assert marks.recording eq true
@assert marks.lastKind eq pending
@assert marks.count eq 1
@assert scene.subtitle.notice eq recording
@assert marks.recordingMs ge 1500
# Nothing pressed: the cap stops it
@until marks.recording eq false 3s
@assert marks.count eq 1
@assert marks.recordingMs eq 0
@until marks.lastKind eq hold 2s
@until marks.lastFiles eq clip.vrsim,left.png,meta.txt,recorder.txt,right.png,snap-+02.0s.jpg,snap-+03.0s.jpg 10s
@assert marks.lastSnapshots eq 2
@assert marks.lastClipMs ge 2900
@assert marks.lastClipMs le 13200
@assert marks.noteMs eq 0
# No snapshot-only mark, no short press, no note (no microphone here)
@nolog \[vr\] mark #\d+: a short press
@nolog files=left\.png,meta\.txt,recorder\.txt,right\.png(?!,)
@nolog note\.wav
# "saved" with the recording's length, and the folder's line, in either order (the files and the notice come from
# the same stop): one look-ahead each
@log (?s)^(?=.*vr\.scene\.subtitle notice=saved [^\n]*text="[^"\n]*[Ss]aved \(0:03\)")(?=.*\[vr\] mark #1: marks\\\d{8}T\d{6}Z-1 files=clip\.vrsim,left\.png,meta\.txt,recorder\.txt,right\.png,snap-\+02\.0s\.jpg,snap-\+03\.0s\.jpg(?!,)) 5s
marks cap 60000
@frames 2
@assert marks.capMs eq 60000

# 3. The clip starts 10 s before the start: at least that much of the session recorded (about 11 s at 90 Hz)
@until vr.sim.timelineFrame ge 1000 30s
@until scene.subtitle.notice eq none 5s

# 4. A recording started by a SHORT press (0.2 s) and stopped by the same press again. The short press is no
# snapshot-only mark any more: it records on after the release. During it the thumbs are free: the left trackpad
# alone (bound to jump here) jumps, the right trackpad alone does nothing to it, the left A opens and closes the bag -
# none of them stops it. The second press of both stops it: no new mark, kind hold, the snapshots at 2 and 4 s and
# the stop (about 4.3-5.5 s), the clip from 10 s before the start to the stop (about 15 s), "saved", then nothing
vr-input bind jump left.trackpad
@frames 2
@assert vr.input.layout.jump eq left.trackpad
@mark
vr-input down left.trackpad; vr-input down right.trackpad
@until marks.count eq 2 1s
@until marks.recording eq true 1s
@wait 200
vr-input up left.trackpad; vr-input up right.trackpad
@until scene.subtitle.notice eq recording 1s
@wait 500
@assert marks.recording eq true
@assert marks.lastKind eq pending
@assert marks.count eq 2
@log vr\.scene\.subtitle notice=recording [^\n]*text="\S+ 0:0\d" 2s
# The left trackpad alone: the game jumps, the recording goes on
@until player.jumping eq false 5s
@remember jumps0 vr.input.presses.jump
vr-input down left.trackpad
@wait 200
vr-input up left.trackpad
@until vr.input.presses.jump eq {jumps0+1} 2s
@assert marks.recording eq true
@assert marks.count eq 2
@assert marks.lastKind eq pending
# The right trackpad alone: the recording goes on
vr-input down right.trackpad
@wait 200
vr-input up right.trackpad
@wait 300
@assert marks.recording eq true
@assert marks.count eq 2
# A button: the left A opens the bag and closes it again, the recording goes on
vr-input tap left.a
@until player.inventoryOpen eq true 5s
@assert marks.recording eq true
vr-input tap left.a
@until player.inventoryOpen eq false 5s
@assert marks.recording eq true
@assert marks.count eq 2
@assert marks.lastKind eq pending
@assert scene.subtitle.notice eq recording
# No mark written yet: nothing of this one in the log, no short press
@nolog \[vr\] mark #2: marks\\
@nolog \[vr\] mark #\d+: a short press
# The second press of both: the stop
@until marks.recordingMs ge 4300 10s
@assert marks.recording eq true
vr-input down left.trackpad; vr-input down right.trackpad
@wait 200
vr-input up left.trackpad; vr-input up right.trackpad
@until marks.recording eq false 2s
@assert marks.count eq 2
@assert marks.recordingMs eq 0
@until marks.lastKind eq hold 2s
@until marks.lastSnapshots eq 3 10s
@until marks.lastClipMs ge 14200 10s
@assert marks.lastClipMs le 16000
@assert marks.count eq 2
@assert marks.noteMs eq 0
@nolog files=left\.png,meta\.txt,recorder\.txt,right\.png(?!,)
@nolog note\.wav
@log (?s)^(?=.*vr\.scene\.subtitle notice=saved [^\n]*text="[^"\n]*[Ss]aved \(0:0[45]\)")(?=.*\[vr\] mark #2: marks\\\d{8}T\d{6}Z-2 files=clip\.vrsim,left\.png,meta\.txt,recorder\.txt,right\.png,snap-\+02\.0s\.jpg,snap-\+04\.0s\.jpg,snap-\+0[45]\.\ds\.jpg(?!,)) 10s
@assert marks.lastSnapshots eq 3
# "saved" fades quickly; the stop press started nothing
@until scene.subtitle.notice eq none 4s
@assert marks.count eq 2
@assert marks.recording eq false

# The default layout back (the trackpads free again)
vr-input default
@frames 2
@assert vr.input.remapped eq false
@assert vr.input.layout.jump eq right.stick_up
@assert errors eq 0
